\par\par \b \uc2 West African Leaders Threaten Force Against Niger Plotters -- WSJ\b0\par\par\uc2 By Drew Hinshaw and Benoit Faucon \par \uc2 1,194 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 Juli 2023\par 20:22\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2023, Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2 West African leaders said that they would consider a military \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to oust coup plotters in Niger and restore democratic rule in a vast Saharan country that they worry could become Russia's newest security partner in the region.\par \par \uc2 At an emergency summit in Nigeria's capital Abuja on Sunday, leaders from the \uc2 Economic Community of West African States\uc2  said Niger's new military junta had one week to return the country's elected president, \uc2 Mohamed Bazoum\uc2 , to power. The regional group, called \uc2 Ecowas\uc2 , also laid out banking and economic sanctions to squeeze the military junta, which on Wednesday detained Bazoum and his family and suspended the country's constitution.\par \par \uc2 "In the event the authorities' demands are not met within one week [\uc2 Ecowas\uc2  will] take all measures necessary to restore constitutional order in the Republic of Niger," Omar Alieu Touray, the president of the \uc2 Ecowas\uc2  commission, said after the meeting. "Such measures may include the use of force."\par \par \uc2 Earlier in the day, thousands of protesters in Niger's capital Niamey marched to the embassy of France -- the country's former colonial ruler -- waving Russian flags, throwing stones and lighting a fire. "FRANCE LEAVE," read several of the crowd's homemade placards. The French military keeps about 1,500 troops in Niger, part of a yearslong campaign against Islamist insurgents in an expansive desert country about twice the size of France itself.\par \par \uc2 The threat of several West African countries \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  with military force in Niger presents an escalation after years of coups that have brought Russian-friendly governments to power in several other nations in the region.\par \par \uc2 Since 2020, military leaders have seized power in Mali and Burkina Faso -- once two of France and the U.S.'s closest counterterrorism partners in West Africa -- shifting those countries' allegiances toward Moscow. Coup leaders have benefited from local frustration that Western militaries, which once parked thousands of troops in the two countries, failed to defeat jihadist insurgencies gaining ground in the region.\par \par \uc2 The coup in Niger verges on a step too far for Nigeria, Africa's most populous country and biggest economy, which shares a 1,000 long-mile border with its northern neighbor. Nigeria's war on its own internal Islamist insurgencies depends on cross-border coordination with Niger.\par \par \uc2 Washington, which has spent more than $500 million dollars equipping and training the local military, also risks losing a partner in the region; U.S. laws restrict such aid to countries under military rule. The \uc2 European Union\uc2 , which has pledged more than 1.5 billion euros, equivalent to about $1.7 billion, in aid for the country since 2017, stands to lose the cooperation of a country that has helped slow the movement of asylum seekers north to Libya and on toward Italy. On Saturday, the \uc2 EU\uc2  said it would freeze some of its support to Niger.\par \par \uc2 Aside from threatening military force, the West African leaders announced a series of banking and trade restrictions that reflected their hope that the junta around Gen. Omar Tchiani, who earlier this week declared himself Niger's new leader, doesn't have the full support of the country's military.\par \par \uc2 The new government of Nigerian President \uc2 Bola Tinubu\uc2  is hoping economic pressure, combined with the threat of force, can get the coup leaders to climb down, a senior Nigerian official said. They are also, the official said, deeply worried about Russia expanding its presence in countries that once looked to their former colonizer France for direction.\par \par \uc2 "It is right now a big power game," he said. "It's between France and Russia."\par \par \uc2 On Saturday, the spokesman for the junta, Col. Maj. Amadou Abdramane, appeared on state TV, saying he wanted to remind "\uc2 Ecowas\uc2 , or any other adventurer, of our fierce determination to defend our homeland."\par \par \uc2 Both the U.S. and Europe have made Niger the centerpiece of their fight against the spread of Islamic State and al Qaeda in Africa's Sahel, the semiarid southern shore of the Sahara. The country hosts American drones and American commandos, who have trained Nigerien special forces, advised them during combat missions, and equipped them with everything from tents and radios to surveillance planes and armored personnel carriers.\par \par \uc2 By contrast, Mali in 2021 hired mercenaries from Russia's \uc2 Wagner group\uc2 , while Burkina Faso earlier this year kicked out French troops\par \par \uc2 French President \uc2 Emmanuel Macron\uc2  condemned the violence at his country's embassy and warned France would respond "immediately and uncompromisingly" to any attack on its citizens, military, diplomats and diplomatic compounds. Immediately after the coup, other protesters in Niamey also came up in support of Bazoum, according to footage posted of his political party's social-media accounts.\par \par \uc2 U.S. and European officials have accused Russia of using disinformation to foster anti-Western sentiment across the Sahel.\par \par \uc2 Beyond threatening a possible military \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the \b \highlight22\uc2 Nigeria\b0 \highlight\uc2 -led group of 15 countries said it would with immediate effect freeze the government's bank accounts in the region's central banks, and in commercial lenders. It also imposed a freeze on all energy-related transactions between Niger and its neighbors. Niger imports more than two-thirds of its electricity from Nigeria.\par \par \uc2 The country uses the same \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  as seven of its West African neighbors, who keep their reserves under a Dakar, Senegal-based \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Those assets should be immediately frozen, \uc2 Ecowas\uc2  said.\par \par \uc2 The bloc would also impose a no-fly zone, and travel bans and asset freezes targeting the plotters if they don't restore Bazoum to power, it said. The measures are similar to those imposed on Mali in 2021 after it failed to respect a plan to move the country toward democratic elections.\par \par \uc2 The banking sanctions will likely have limited impact on Niger, where the overwhelming majority of citizens are unbanked, and could backfire by allowing Russia to step in as a new patron for the country's coup leaders, said Bismarck Rewane, managing director of Lagos research firm Financial Derivatives Co.\par \par \uc2 "It will have an impact ostracizing them, but it doesn't do that much," he said. "It's a nice sound bite...The big fear is what it opens up for the Russians."\par \par \uc2 Some African nations, however, still hope the standoff in Niger could end peacefully.\par \par \uc2 Mahamat Deby, the transitional president of Chad, met Salifou Modi, one of the Niger junta leaders, in Niamey Sunday, in an attempt to resolve the crisis, Chad's information minister Aziz Mahamat Saleh said. The Chadian official said the visit followed consultations with Nigeria.\par \par \uc2 Bazoum has refused to step down or leave his residence, where he has been held hostage for five days by the coup plotters. "He is serene and says he had no intention to resign," says Ange Barou Chekaraou, a leader in Bazoum's Nigerien Party for Democracy and Socialism, who has spoken to him on the phone.\par \par \uc2 --Gbenga Akingbule and Noemie Bisserbe contributed to this article.\par \par \uc2 Write to Drew Hinshaw at drew.hinshaw@wsj.com and Benoit Faucon at benoit.faucon@wsj.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 July 30, 2023 14:22 ET (18:22 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020230730ej7u0007f\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
