\par\par \b \uc2 African Markets - Factors to watch on July 28\b0\par\par\uc2 499 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Juli 2022\par 06:42\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     NAIROBI, July 28 (Reuters) - The following company announcements, scheduled economic\par indicators, debt and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market moves and political events may affect African markets on\par Thursday.\par                      - - - - -\par  EVENTS:\par  ETHIOPIA - State-owned \f28 \uc2 \f2 Ethio Telecom\f28 \uc2 \f2  releases financial results for the year to end-June.\par  \par  GLOBAL MARKETS\par  Asian shares made cautious gains on Thursday as investors scented a possible slowdown in\par  the pace of U.S. rate hikes, comforting bond markets and sending the dollar to a\par  three-week low on the yen.                       \par  \par  WORLD OIL PRICES\par  Oil gained more than $1 a barrel on Thursday, extending gains from the previous session,\par  buoyed by improved risk appetite among investors while lower crude inventories and a\par  rebound in gasoline demand in the United States supported prices.                 \par  \par  EMERGING MARKETS\par  For the top emerging markets news, double click on            \par  \par  AFRICA STOCKS\par  For the latest news on African stocks, click on     \par  \par  SOUTH AFRICA MARKETS\par  South Africa's rand firmed on Wednesday ahead of an interest rate hike decision by the\par  \f28 \uc2 \f2 U.S. Federal Reserve\f28 \uc2 \f2  due later in the day.            \par  \par  NIGERIA \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CENTRAL BANK\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par  Nigeria's Senate passed a motion on Wednesday to summon \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Governor \f28 \uc2 \f2 Godwin\par  Emefiele\f28 \uc2 \f2  over the "free fall of the naira" and called on the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to urgently\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .            \par  \par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 NIGERIA\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  CRUDE OIL REVENUES\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Nigeria\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has had no accretion to its rainy day oil savings account in the past four years,\par  Finance Minister \f28 \uc2 \f2 Zainab Ahmed\f28 \uc2 \f2  said on Wednesday, citing volatility on oil\par  markets.            \par  \par  NIGERIA POLITICS\par  Nigerian opposition Senators pushed for President \f28 \uc2 \f2 Muhammadu Buhari\f28 \uc2 \f2  to face impeachment,\par  10-months before the end of his second term in office, over the country's spreading\par  security problems, the Senate minority leader said on Wednesday.            \par  \par  KENYA MARKETS\par  Kenya's shilling        was little-changed on Wednesday, and traders said they expected\par  it to weaken due to increased dollar demand from various sectors, especially oil\par  importers.            \par  \par  \f28 \uc2 \f2 KENYA \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CENTRAL BANK\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  LENDING RATE\par  \f28 \uc2 \f2 Kenya's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  held its benchmark lending rate              at 7.5% on Wednesday to\par  allow May's hike to transmit its way through the economy, its monetary policy committee\par  (MPC) said.                  \par  \par  KENYA EAST AFRICAN BREWERIES RESULTS\par  Kenya's East African Breweries           said on Thursday its pretax profit for the year\par  to end-June more than doubled, helped by improving sales as COVID-19 curbs eased in its\par  markets.             \par  \par  RIO TINTO GUINEA\par  Rio Tinto        ,          said on Thursday that its Guinea subsidiary has formed a\par  joint venture with the government and the Winning Consortium Simandou (WCS), paving the\par  way for work to resume at the world\u8217\'20\'19s largest underdeveloped iron ore\par  deposit.                   \par  \par  BOTSWANA TAX\par  Botswana has cut value added tax (VAT) by 2 percentage points to 12% for a six-month\par  period as part of measures to cushion consumers from the prevailing high inflation rate,\par  Finance Minister Peggy Serame told parliament on Wednesday.            \par  \par      For the latest precious metals report click on        \par      For the latest base metals report click on         \par      For the latest crude oil report click on\f28 \par \par \uc2 Released: 2022-7-28T05:42:09.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020220728ei7s00odu\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
