\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1- \highlight22\uc2 Nigeria central bank \highlight \highlight22\uc2 intervening \highlight\uc2  to prop up naira, trader says\b0\par\par\uc2 326 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 August 2019\par 14:19\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2019 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 (Adds quotes, details)\par \par \uc2 By Chijioke Ohuocha\par \par \uc2 LAGOS, Aug 1 (Reuters) - The \uc2 Nigerian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market over the past two weeks to keep the naira stable as foreign investors took profits after yields fell on the local debt market, a trader told Reuters.\par \par \uc2 The naira was quoted at 362.80 to the dollar on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market for investors, weaker than the level around 361 level where it has traded for much of this year, said the dealer, who trades \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  for the local unit of an international bank.\par \par \uc2 Pressure has been building on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  amid a dwindling supply of dollars. It now takes more than a week to fill customer orders.\par \par \uc2 Nigeria operates a multiple exchange rate regime. It maintains an official exchange rate of 306 naira to the dollar, supported by \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The traded rate of 362.80 is the one widely quoted by foreign investors and exporters.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  does not disclose how many dollars it injects into the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market.\par \par \uc2 "We are currently seeing more outflow than inflow ... but the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," the trader said. "The moment the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  doesn't provide support, people may start to panic."\par \par \uc2 Nigeria's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has cut back on open market auctions to attract foreign investors in its bonds, a policy shift aimed at stimulating lending to boost an economy stuck with low growth after a recent recession.\par \par \uc2 The bank auctioned a one-year open-market bill last month at around 12%, down from as high as 18% a year ago.\par \par \uc2 The trader said some offshore clients were taking profits and that summer holidays in Europe could also account for the low volumes.\par \par \uc2 "If local rates were much higher, I don't think we would have seen much outflows." (Reporting by Chijioke Ohuocha, editing by Larry King) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2019-8-1T13:19:39.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020190801ef8102gw1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
