\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2-\uc2 Nigeria  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight\uc2  may reduce $8.1 bln MTN repatriation demand\b0\par\par\uc2 415 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Oktober 2018\par 16:36\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2018 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 (Adds quotes, background)\par \par \uc2 By Karin Strohecker\par \par \uc2 LONDON, Oct 7 (Reuters) - The \uc2 Nigerian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may reduce the amount it has ordered South African telecoms firm MTN to repatriate as part of an ongoing disagreement, \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor \uc2 Godwin Emefiele\uc2  said on Sunday.\par \par \uc2 MTN and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  are in a dispute over the transfer of $8.1 billion of funds which the bank said the company had sent abroad in breach of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  regulations. Nigeria accounts for a third of MTN's annual core profit.\par \par \uc2 "I don't think it will be staying at $8.1 billion," Emefiele said during a visit to London, adding he expected the issue to be dealt with "amicably and equitably".\par \par \uc2 "I want to believe that the figures will reduce. Whether they will be dropped completely, I honestly cannot say at this time."\par \par \uc2 Emefiele said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had received documents some two weeks ago from MTN and four lenders involved in the case - \uc2 Standard Chartered\uc2 , \uc2 Stanbic IBTC Bank\uc2 , \uc2 Citibank\uc2  and \uc2 Diamond Bank\uc2  - and was in communications with all parties involved.\par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will be examining these, then it will be escalated up to my level," he said, adding he expected to get the results in a couple of weeks.\par \par \uc2 The two sides are locked in a court dispute over the transaction. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  filed a counter-claim on Friday to a court request by MTN, which is seeking to stop the bank from forcing it to bring back the money.\par \par \uc2 Emefiele said the MTN case was a one-off, and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was not looking at transactions involving any other companies operating in Nigeria.\par \par \uc2 "We respect the sanctity of these companies," he said.\par \par \uc2 Shares in MTN lost almost 5 percent over the past week.\par \par \uc2 Emefiele also said \b \highlight22\uc2 Nigeria\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would continue to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, adding that he believed in a stable exchange rate regime.\par \par \uc2 Nigeria has been battling to defend its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and shore up its reserves of around $44 billion, hobbled by lower oil prices. At the same time, the oil exporter has suffered from high inflation, which edged up to 11.2 percent at its last reading - well above the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's 6-9 percent target.\par \par \uc2 Emefiele said Nigeria's current stance of monetary tightening would continue. (Reporting by Karin Strohecker; Writing by Jan Harvey; Editing by Dale Hudson) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2018-10-7T15:36:38.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020181007eea700lap\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
