\par\par \b \uc2 Nigeria's  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight\uc2  boosts  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  sales to ease pressure on naira\b0\par\par\uc2 381 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 August 2018\par 20:25\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2018 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 ABUJA, Aug 24 (Reuters) - \uc2 Nigeria's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  stepped up dollar sales this week after it auctioned the U.S. and Chinese \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  last week in a bid to alleviate shortages and ease pressure on the naira.\par \par \uc2 On Friday the bank said it sold a total of $543.22 million on the interbank market and another 63.21 million yuan ($9.20 million) to settle letters of credit denominated in the Chinese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  via spot and forward contracts, it said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 Last week the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  asked lenders to submit bids for the Chinese yuan, its second auction of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  after it agreed a swap with the \uc2 People's Bank of China\uc2  in May to boost trade between the two countries and cut reliance on the dollar.\par \par \uc2 It sold $210 million on Thursday and $323.22 million on Friday after a dollar auction last week, the bank said.\par \par \uc2 Isaac Okorafor\uc2 , \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  spokesperson said "the bank remained committed to maintaining the country's external reserves to safeguard the international value of the naira."\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  typically sells between $200 million and $300 million when it enters the interbank market, traders said.\par \par \uc2 However, dollar liquidity has been shrinking as a result of capital reversals after the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  started to raise interest rates this year.\par \par \uc2 Trading was quiet this week as the little quantity of hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold by local exporters was unable to meet demand, traders said, with importers bidding repeatedly to try to fill their request.\par \par \uc2 The naira has been quoted as weak as 364 per dollar for investors this week after trading within a range of 362 to 363. On the official market, supported by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , it was quoted at 306.10.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said the naira was trading at 360 per dollar at exchange bureaus and the yuan sold for 53.17 naira.\par \par \uc2 It attributed the relative stable exchange rate to its \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  as well as higher global oil prices. \b \highlight22\uc2 Nigeria\b0 \highlight\uc2  operates a multiple exchange rate regime which it has used to manage demand for hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . ($1 = 6.8740 Chinese yuan renminbi) (Reporting by Camillus Eboh and Chijioke Ohuocha; Editing by Toby Chopra) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2018-8-24T19:25:54.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020180824ee8o02up9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
