\par\par \b \uc2 Nigeria naira eases as investors repatriate dividend\b0\par\par\uc2 336 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Mai 2018\par 18:48\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2018 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 LAGOS, May 8 (Reuters) - Nigeria's naira eased to 362 to the dollar for investors on Tuesday as funds repatriate dividends abroad following the end of the earnings season and as forward \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  contracts mature amid tight dollar liquidity, traders said.\par \par \uc2 The naira traded at 360 for over six months after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  in April 2017 liberalised the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  for investors in the wake of a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  crisis brought on by low oil prices that also slashed government revenues.\par \par \uc2 Traders said the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  started to weaken last week as demand piled up especially from companies seeking to repatriate dividends and investors booking profits from local assets.\par \par \uc2 Importers buying goods from abroad were also exerting pressure on the naira.\par \par \uc2 Nigeria emerged from its first recession in a quarter of a century last year but growth is still fragile. It then introduced a multiple exchange rate regime to manage dollar demand as a way to alleviate chronic shortages on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets.\par \par \uc2 On the official market the naira is quoted at around 305 per dollar, a level it has been for over a year, supported by \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's regular \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 MTN's \b \highlight22\uc2 Nigeria operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  declared a dividend of 50 billion naira ($159 mln) by its local unit in 2017, a company presentation seen by Reuters showed, which Africa's biggest telecom group would seek to repatriate to offshore investors. MTN further paid a dividend in the first quarter, it said.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is gradually loosening policy to adopt a more dovish stance on interest rates especially as its foreign reserves are rising, giving the West African country a buffer with which to defend the naira.\par \par \uc2 The bank has reduced its issuance of open market bills to tighten naira liquidity, traders said with banking system liquidity closing at around 200 billion naira in credit on Monday, to lower treasury yields.\par \par \uc2 ($1 = 314.50 naira) (Reporting by Chijioke Ohuocha Editing by Richard Balmforth) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2018-5-8T17:48:38.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020180508ee5800mgq\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
