\par\par \b \uc2 EXCLUSIVE-UPDATE 2-Nigeria's people getting poorer, govt to "muddle through", says \uc2 IMF\b0\par\par\uc2 546 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Februar 2018\par 20:07\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2018 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 (Adds details)\par \par \uc2 By Paul Carsten\par \par \uc2 LAGOS, Feb 28 (Reuters) - Nigeria's people are getting poorer despite the country's slow recovery from recession, and economic reforms are urgently needed, the \uc2 International Monetary Fund\uc2  (\uc2 IMF\uc2 ) said in a report seen by Reuters on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 The Fund expects the government to "muddle through" in the medium term, and any progress could also be threatened if elections next year consume political energy and resources, the report said.\par \par \uc2 Since emerging from recession in the second quarter of 2017, Nigerian officials have repeatedly boasted that they have set the economy back on track.\par \par \uc2 But critics say much of the recovery comes from a return to oil dependence after a rise in global oil prices and a rebound in crude production - more the result of militants in the Niger Delta halting attacks on oil facilities than of economic policy under President \uc2 Muhammadu Buhari\uc2 's administration.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 IMF\uc2  said in the report that the outlook for growth has improved but remains challenging.\par \par \uc2 "Comprehensive and coherent" economic policies "remain urgent and must not be delayed by approaching elections and recovering oil prices," it said in its annual Article IV review of Nigeria's economy.\par \par \uc2 "Higher oil prices would support a recovery in 2018 but a 'muddle-through' outlook is projected for the medium term under current policies, with fiscal dominance and structural constraints leading to continuing falls in real GDP per capita," the \uc2 IMF\uc2  said.\par \par \uc2 In the report, it identified risks to growth including additional delays to implementing policies and reforms ahead of 2019 elections, security tensions, and oil prices, a fall in which could see capital flows reversed.\par \par \uc2 "Further delays in policy action -- including because of pre-election pressures -- can only make the inevitable adjustment more difficult and costlier," the report said.\par \par \uc2 EXCHANGE RATE CONFUSION\par \par \uc2 The lender repeated its call for Nigeria to simplify its complex \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  system, a bugbear for the \uc2 IMF\uc2  for more than a year which has left large gaps between official rates and various windows that certain groups can use to get other rates.\par \par \uc2 "Moving towards a unified exchange rate should be pursued as soon as possible," the \uc2 IMF\uc2  said. "(\uc2 IMF\uc2 ) staff does not support the exchange measures that have given rise to the exchange restrictions and multiple \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  practices."\par \par \uc2 The Fund further singled out the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , saying it should discontinue direct \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the economy.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Nigeria\b0 \highlight\uc2  (CBN) \uc2 frequently injects hundreds of millions of dollars into the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to keep its own rates stable.\par \par \uc2 Commercial banks struggling to remain solvent were also called out, but not identified by the \uc2 IMF\uc2 , including one that the lender said was already insolvent: "Some of these banks are kept afloat through continuous recourse to the CBN's lending facilities."\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 IMF\uc2  said it does not comment on purported leaks. A spokeswoman for the Fund said a statement would be issued after the lender's board meets to discuss its assessment on Friday.\par \par \uc2 A \uc2 Nigerian finance ministry\uc2  spokeswoman did not immediately respond to a phone call and email requesting comment. (Reporting by Paul Carsten; Additional reporting by Chijioke Ohuocha; Editing by Catherine Evans and Hugh Lawson) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2018-2-28T20:07:12.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020180228ee2s00qxw\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
