\par\par \b \uc2 Nigeria naira eases on black market as dollar demand resurfaces\b0\par\par\uc2 310 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 August 2017\par 18:36\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2017 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 LAGOS, Aug 23 (Reuters) - Nigerian naira fell on the black market on Wednesday, pressured by demand for dollars from Muslim pilgrims travelling to Saudi Arabia for the haj and individuals paying for school fees abroad.\par \par \uc2 The naira was quoted at 370 to the dollar on the black market on Wednesday as against 368 naira its previous session, traders said.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has traded within a range of 359 to 366 naira to the dollar for investors and on the parallel market over the past two weeks. It is stuck at around 305 levels on the official market boosted by \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Nigeria\b0 \highlight\uc2  has at least five exchange rates -- including for the haj -- which it has used to mask pressure on the naira. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been working to converge the rates through regular dollar sales.\par \par \uc2 On Wednesday the bank announced that it will sell the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to clear backlog demand for airlines and to importers of petroleum products and raw materials.\par \par \uc2 Traders said demand has resurfaced in the past one week as private individuals with certain expenses in hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  source for dollars.\par \par \uc2 Nigeria's parliament in July recommended that Muslim pilgrims travelling to Saudi Arabia this year should be able to buy their dollars for 200 naira, far below the official rate.\par \par \uc2 Aminu Gwadabe, president of the Bureau de Change operators told Reuters that pressure was coming from pilgrims travelling for haj and that \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had not granted any concessions.\par \par \uc2 Gwadabe said dollar liquidity among exchange bureaus was low as some of his members refused to participate at a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  auction over tight margins as the regulator tries to converge the different rates on offer. (Reporting by Oludare Mayowa; Editing by Chijioke Ohuocha/Jeremy Gaunt) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2017-8-23T17:36:36.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020170823ed8n00lj4\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw90\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1350\pichgoal600
