     41          -    \par                                                  1 026          246        348    \par     Iran - major joint venture                       -         (294)       326    \par                                                                                  \par \par 6.  SEGMENT ANALYSIS\par     The Group has identified reportable segments that are used by the Group executive committee (chief operating decision \par     maker (CODM)) to make key operating decisions, allocate resources and assess performance. The reportable segments \par     are grouped according to their geographic locations.\par \par     The \f28 \uc2 \f2 MTN Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  is clustered into the following three regions and their respective underlying \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 :\par     - South and East Africa (SEA)\par     - West and Central Africa (WECA)\par     - Middle East and North Africa (MENA).\par \par     Operating results are reported and reviewed regularly by the CODM and include external transactions or transactions \par     with other Group segments that can be attributable to a segment on a reasonable basis.\par \par     EBITDA is used as the measure of reporting profit or loss for each segment and represents the basis on which the \par     CODM reviews segment results. It is defined as earnings before interest, tax, depreciation, amortisation, impairment \par     of goodwill, net monetary gains and share of results of joint ventures and associates after tax and further excludes \par     the following items:\par     - Hyperinflation (note 5)\par     - Tower sale and exchange right profit on \f28 \uc2 \f2 IHS\f28 \uc2 \f2  investment (note 7)\par     - Nigeria regulatory fine (note 8)\par     - \f28 \uc2 \f2 MTN Zakhele\f28 \uc2 \f2  Futhi share-based payment expense.\par \par     Other than for the exclusion of the exchange right profit on the \f28 \uc2 \f2 IHS\f28 \uc2 \f2  investment during the period under review (note 7), \par     this measure has remained unchanged in comparison to prior periods.\par \par     Irancell Telecommunication Company Services (PJSC) (Iran) proportionate results are included in the segment analysis \par     as reviewed by the CODM and excluded from IFRS reported results for revenue, EBITDA and capex due to equity accounting \par     for joint ventures. The results of Iran in the segment analysis exclude the impact of hyperinflation accounting.                 \par     \par                                                                                      Financial    \par                                                  Six months       Six months              year    \par                             ended            ended             ended    \par                                                     30 June          30 June       31 December    \par                                                        2017             2016              2016    \par                                                    Reviewed         Reviewed           Audited    \par             Note           Rm               Rm                Rm    \par     REVENUE                                                                                     \par     SEA                                              24 767           25 156            52 142    \par     South Africa                                     20 156           19 841            41 922    \par     Uganda                  2 506            2 804             5 465    \par     Other SEA                                         2 105            2 511             4 755    \par     WECA                                             33 308           46 347            80 655    \par     Nigeria                                          18 037           28 941            47 122    \par     Ghana              4 864            5 165            10 291    \par     Cameroon                                          2 609            3