ar     general banking facilities and R757 million (June 2016: R2 billion, December 2016: R2,1 billion) through \par     the Domestic Medium Term Programme.\par \par     MTN Holdings repaid R2,0 billion (June 2016: R800 million, December 2016: R7,4 billion) of the syndicated \par     loan facility, R3,2 billion (June 2016: R1,2 billion, December 2016: R2,9 billion) of general banking facilities \par     and R746 million (June 2016: R nil, December 2016: R154 million) of the Domestic Medium Term Programme. \par \par     MTN International (Mauritius) Limited (MTN Mauritius) raised R1,3 billion (June 2016: R3,5 billion, \par     December 2016: R11,2 billion) and repaid R nil (June 2016: R837 million, December 2016: R12,9 billion) \par     on a revolving credit facility. \par \par     MTN Nigeria Communications Limited raised R1,5 billion (June 2016: R nil, December 2016: R nil) long-term \par     borrowings and repaid R2,1 billion (June 2016: R3,2 billion, December 2016: R5,4 billion).\par     \par     Other borrowings raised and repaid across the Group amounted to R1,3 billion (June 2016: R6,8 billion, \par     December 2016: R12 billion) and R4,1 billion (June 2016: R4,4 billion, December 2016: R8,4 billion), \par     respectively.\par \par     During the second half of 2016, MTN (Mauritius) Investments Limited raised R14,2 billion debt through \par     long-term fixed interest rate unsecured notes. These notes are listed on the Irish Stock Exchange.\par \par                                                                                  Financial    \par                                   Six months             Six months                   year    \par                                        ended                  ended                  ended    \par                                      30 June                30 June            31 December    \par                                         2017                   2016                   2016    \par                       