\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Nigerian banks seek \uc2 Etisalat Nigeria\uc2  cash flow clarity before results\b0\par\par\uc2 534 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Juli 2017\par 20:48\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2017 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 (Adds announcement of name change, paragraph 5)\par \par \uc2 By Chijioke Ohuocha\par \par \uc2 LAGOS, July 13 (Reuters) - \uc2 Etisalat Nigeria\uc2 's rescue has put the country's banks in a quandary as they prepare for half-year results due this month as they do not know whether to provision for loans to the company until they can work out its value.\par \par \uc2 A banking source told Reuters that the lenders first wanted to determine \uc2 Etisalat Nigeria\uc2 's free cash flow to help them value the telecoms business before deciding on whether to impair the assets or hold on to find new investors.\par \par \uc2 "No bank is talking about restructuring now, but it might get to that later once we are able to ascertain the true value of the company," the source said.\par \par \uc2 Nigerian regulators \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  last week to save \uc2 Etisalat \b \highlight22\uc2 Nigeria\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the country's fourth-largest mobile operator, from collapse and prevent lenders placing the telecoms firm in receivership, prompting a board and management change.\par \par \uc2 On Thursday, \uc2 Etisalat Nigeria\uc2  changed its name to 9mobile, the company said.\par \par \uc2 The telecoms firm took-out a $1.2 billion loan four years ago from 13 local lenders to refinance an existing debt and expand its mobile network, but it struggled to repay due a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  crisis and recession in Nigeria.\par \par \uc2 Banks involved in the loan deal include: \uc2 Zenith Bank\uc2  , \uc2 GT Bank\uc2 , \uc2 First Bank\uc2 , UBA , \uc2 Fidelity Bank\uc2 , \uc2 Access Bank\uc2 , Ecobank, FCMB, \uc2 Stanbic IBTC Bank\uc2  and \uc2 Union Bank\uc2 . Results are due from this month.\par \par \uc2 GT Bank\uc2  with $138 million in outstanding loans and \uc2 Access Bank\uc2  with $131 million are among the most exposed to \uc2 Etisalat Nigeria\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "We think that by the time the new management settles in, makes some changes and reduces costs, the company might bounce back," the source told Reuters, adding that he expected support from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which has sought to avoid \uc2 Etisalat Nigeria\uc2 's collapse from sparking a wider debt crisis.\par \par \uc2 Etisalat Nigeria\uc2 's new chief executive Boye Olusanya told Reuters on Tuesday he was focused on getting the telecoms group back on track to make a profit, while working on the paperwork to eventually raise new capital.\par \par \uc2 Renaissance Capital analysts estimates \uc2 Etisalat Nigeria\uc2  could be worth $1.2 billion based on an enterprise value to operating cashflow multiple when compared with South Africa's MTN and other African telecoms companies.\par \par \uc2 Nigeria's banks are set to report interim earnings this month and investors will be watching for signs of a rise in non-performing loans.\par \par \uc2 The banks collected half of their interest payment for May from \uc2 Etisalat Nigeria\uc2  so that the new team running the company has funds to keep it operating, the source said.\par \par \uc2 And any provisioning may not kick in until the next quarter.\par \par \uc2 "Given the understanding that Etisalat's debt was performing till the end of the first quarter we believe the banks ... might be required to make provisions in the second quarter," said Olalekan Olabode, head of research at Vetiva Capital said.\par \par \uc2 "Rather than converting the debt to equity, we expect to see a restructuring in the near term," he added.\par \par \uc2 (Editing by Alexander Smith and Edmund Blair) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2017-7-13T19:48:04.000Z \par \par \uc2 