\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2-\uc2 Nigerian  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight\uc2  trying to make  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  rates converge -spokesman\b0\par\par\uc2 406 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 Mai 2017\par 17:10\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2017 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 (Adds \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  volume on spot market, sales to firms)\par \par \uc2 By Oludare Mayowa and Chijioke Ohuocha\par \par \uc2 LAGOS, May 2 (Reuters) - \uc2 Nigeria's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is working to make exchange rates for its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  converge on the official and black markets, its spokesman said, and plans to offer $100 million on the forward market on Tuesday to boost liquidity.\par \par \uc2 Nigeria runs a system of multiple exchange rates, and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has sold more than $4 billion on the spot and forward markets in its efforts to increase liquidity. In theory, greater liquidity should lead the rates to converge.\par \par \uc2 The naira was quoted weaker on Tuesday at an investor trading window, at 380.31 per dollar, data from market regulator FMDQ OTC Securities Exchange showed. The official market rate was 305.85 and the black-market rate 390.\par \par \uc2 On the spot interbank market, the naira traded a total of $51.68 million, volumes last seen in October 2016.\par \par \uc2 "The bank is committed and is indeed working to achieve convergence in the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates between the interbank and the bureau de change segment," said spokesman Isaac Okorafor.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said all dollar allotments must be backed by demand and that it will settle Tuesday's dollar sale between one week and 45 days after the sale.\par \par \uc2 It then said it would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  with an undisclosed amount to clear a backlog of demand for airlines, raw materials and machinery and that it would debit the companies for the naira equivalent of the dollar amount immediately.\par \par \uc2 The bank offered $100 million last Thursday but ended up selling $85.69 million. Okorafor said in a statement lenders did not take up the whole offer as there was "enough \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  to meet legitimate demand".\par \par \uc2 Analysts doubt whether the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  can sustain such sales. The convoluted exchange rate system masks pressure on the naira with the regulator trying to avoid a devaluation.\par \par \uc2 Okorafor said the bank has the capacity to sustain its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Nigeria\b0 \highlight\uc2 's dollar reserves grew to a 19-month high of $30.8 billion last week, thanks to a recent rise in global oil prices, the country's main source of hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . But reserves remain far off the peak of $64 billion reached in August 2008. (Additional reporting by Camillus Eboh in Abuja; Writing by Chijioke Ohuocha; Editing by Mark Heinrich) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2017-5-2T16:10:15.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020170502ed5200dz0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
