\par\par \b \uc2 Nigeria ETF Lower: 14% Interest Rate On Hold -- Barron's Blog\b0\par\par\uc2 By Dimitra DeFotis \par \uc2 371 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2017\par 17:28\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2017, Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2 The iShares MSCI Nigeria exchange-traded fund ( NGE) was down 1.4% in midday trading after the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  kept its 14% policy interest rate on hold.\par \par \uc2 The oil-dependent country is struggling with stubbornly low crude prices, and inflation is taking a bite out of consumer's wallets. Economist John Ashbourne at \uc2 Capital Economics\uc2  writes:\par \par \uc2 "The accompanying statement hinted, however, that policymakers are finally considering the case for tightening policy in the face of above-target inflation. ... The communication was, as ever, a bit unclear. We do not expect a meaningful shift in policy anytime soon ... The [\b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ] governor spent much of his time discussing global factors that have limited relevance for Nigeria. Of the various factors that can be blamed for Nigeria's economic troubles, it is far from clear that protectionist rhetoric in the US has played a significant role. The Governor also provided little clarity on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  issue. There was no further information about the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Nigeria\b0 \highlight\uc2 's recent \b \highlight22\uc2 FX interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which have created a whole new exchange rate and caused the widely used parallel rate to appreciate against the USD ...\par \par \uc2 The governor's stated objection that tighter rates would "portray the bank as insensitive" to concerns about growth was, however, more worrying. First, it is not clear that looser policy will provide much of a boost to growth in Nigeria's economy, which has been held back by a deteriorating security situation an falling oil output. Second, concerns about how the bank would be "portrayed" seem to ignore the CBN's primary mandate of achieving price stability, to which the governor referred in the same speech. Yet again, policymakers' statements have provided little clarity ..."\par \par \uc2 See our posts Nigeria's Trade Dilemma: Dirty Oil Or Expensive Fuel, Nigeria Political Change: Chaos or Oil Boost? and Nigeria: Is A Recovery Ahead?\par \par \uc2 Nigeria is exempt from \uc2 OPEC\uc2  oil cuts required of members through June. See our post Oil Investments Sink On \uc2 OPEC\uc2 , Saudi Data. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  More at Barron's Emerging Markets blog, \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://blogs.barrons.com/emergingmarketsdaily/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://blogs.barrons.com/emergingmarketsdaily/}}}\par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 March 21, 2017 12:28 ET (16:28 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020170321ed3l002d8\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
