\par\par \b \uc2 *S&PGR Maintains Its Suspension Of Nigerian Skye Bank Ratings\b0\par\par\uc2 1,817 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2017\par 17:58\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2017, Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2 2 Mar 2017 11:58 ET  Press Release: S&PGR Maintains Its Suspension Of Nigerian Skye Bank Ratings\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par The following is a press release from \f28 \uc2 \f2 Standard & Poor's\f28 \uc2 \f2 : \par  \par      -- We are continuing to suspend our ratings on Nigeria-based \f28 \uc2 \f2 Skye Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2  \par due to the ongoing lack of sufficient, reliable, and timely information. \par      -- The suspension is expected to be for 90 days, pending the receipt of \par further information. \par  \par JOHANNESBURG (S&P Global Ratings) March 2, 2017--S&P Global Ratings today \par maintained its suspension of its counterparty credit ratings and national \par scale ratings on \f28 \uc2 \f2 Skye Bank PLC\f28 \uc2 \f2 . \par  \par We initially suspended the ratings on Dec. 6, 2016 (see "Nigeria's Skye Bank \par Ratings Suspended Due To Lack of Sufficient Information," published on \par RatingsDirect). At the time of the suspension, the 'CCC-/C' global scale \par ratings and 'ngCCC-/ngC' Nigeria national scale ratings were on CreditWatch \par with negative implications. \par  \par The suspension is based on a lack of sufficient, timely, and reliable \par information to maintain our ratings on \f28 \uc2 \f2 Skye Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2 . We were informed that the \par bank will delay the publication of its 2016 half-year financial information in \par order to cover the whole 12 months ending Dec. 31, 2016. \par  \par At midyear 2016, the bank breached some regulatory ratios, including the \par minimum capital adequacy and liquidity ratios, which led the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of \par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Nigeria\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , suspending the bank's board of directors and changing \par its top management on July 4, 2016. \par  \par Since then, the quality, quantity, and timeliness of information that we have \par received from the bank continues to fall short of our requirements, resulting \par in our decision to suspend the ratings. At the time of suspension, we \par understood from our interaction with the bank's management that \f28 \uc2 \f2 Skye Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2  had \par been making timely payments on funding facilities and deposits both in U.S. \par dollars and Nigerian naira. We also understood that the bank has restructured \par some off-balance-sheet trade-related facilities under mutually agreed \par conditions with creditors. \par  \par We expect to be able to resolve the suspension within the next 90 days, \par subject to receiving the necessary information from the bank. If the \par information is not sufficient, we may withdraw our ratings. \par  \par RELATED CRITERIA \par  \par      -- General Criteria: S&P Global Ratings' National And Regional Scale \par Mapping Tables, June 01, 2016 \par      -- General Criteria: National And Regional Scale Credit Ratings, Sept. \par 22, 2014 \par      -- General Criteria: Group Rating Methodology, Nov. 19, 2013 \par      -- Criteria - Financial Institutions - Banks: Quantitative Metrics For \par Rating Banks Globally: Methodology And Assumptions, July 17, 2013 \par      -- General Criteria: Criteria For Assigning 'CCC+', 'CCC', 'CCC-', And \par 'CC' Ratings, Oct. 01, 2012 \par      -- Criteria - Financial Institutions - Banks: Revised Market Risk Charges \par For Banks In Our Risk-Adjusted Capital Framework, June 22, 2012 \par      -- Criteria - Financial Institutions - Banks: Banks: Rating Methodology \par And Assumptions, Nov. 09, 2011 \par      -- Criteria - Financial Institutions - Banks: Banking Industry Country \par Risk Assessment Methodology And Assumptions, Nov. 09, 2011 \par      -- Criteria - Financial Institutions - Banks: Bank Capital Methodology \par And Assumptions, Dec. 06, 2010 \par      -- General Criteria: Understanding Standard & Poor's Rating Definitions, \par June 03, 2009 \par      -- Criteria - Financial Institutions - Banks: Commercial Paper I: Banks, \par March 23, 2004 \par  \par RELATED RESEARCH \par      -- Nigeria's Skye Bank Ratings Suspended Due To Lack of Sufficient \par Information, Dec. 6, 2016 \par      -- Nigeria Bank Outlook 2017: Economic And \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Concerns Will Fuel \par Weaker Capital And Higher Credit Losses, Feb. 27, 2017 \par  \par REGULATORY DISCLOSURES \par      -- Primary Credit Analyst: Matthew Pirnie, Director \par      -- Rating Committee Chairperson: John Gibling \par      -- Date initial rating assigned: Aug. 7, 2013 \par      -- Date of previous review: Dec. 6, 2016 \par  \par DISCLAIMERS \par This rating has been determined by a rating committee based solely on the \par committee's independent evaluation of the credit risks and merits of the \par issuer or issue being rated in accordance with S&P Global Ratings published \par criteria and no part of this rating was influenced by any other business \par activities of S&P Global Ratings. \par  \par This credit rating is solicited. The rated entity did participate in the \par credit rating process. S&P Global Ratings did have access to the accounts, \par financial records and other relevant internal, non-public documents of the \par rated entity or a related third party. S&P Global Ratings has used information \par from sources believed to be reliable but does not guarantee the accuracy, \par adequacy, or completeness of any information used. \par  \par GLOSSARY \par      -- Counterparty credit rating: A form of issuer credit rating, which is a \par forward-looking opinion about an obligor's overall creditworthiness. \par      -- Credit losses: Losses arising from credit risk. \par      -- Credit risk: Risk that a borrower will default on its payment \par obligations. \par      -- Customer loans (gross): Total customer loans before loan loss reserves. \par      -- Date initial rating assigned: The date S&P Global Ratings assigned the \par long-term foreign \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  issuer credit rating on the entity. \par      -- Date of previous review: The date S&P Global Ratings last reviewed the \par credit rating on the entity. \par      -- National scale rating: An opinion of an obligor's creditworthiness or \par overall capacity to meet specific financial obligations, relative to other \par issuers and issues in a given country or region. \par  \par Certain terms used in this report, particularly certain adjectives used to \par express our view on rating relevant factors, have specific meanings ascribed \par to them in our criteria, and should therefore be read in conjunction with such \par criteria. Please see Ratings Criteria at \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.standardandpoors.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 www.standardandpoors.com}}}\uc2 \f2  for further \par information. Complete ratings information is available to subscribers of \par RatingsDirect at \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.globalcreditportal.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 www.globalcreditportal.com}}}\uc2 \f2  and at spcapitaliq.com. All \par ratings affected by this rating action can be found on the S&P Global Ratings' \par public website at \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.standardandpoors.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 www.standardandpoors.com}}}\uc2 \f2 . Use the Ratings search box located \par in the left column.  Alternatively, call one of the following S&P Global \par Ratings numbers: Client Support Europe (44) 20-7176-7176; London Press Office \par (44) 20-7176-3605; Paris (33) 1-4420-6708; Frankfurt (49) 69-33-999-225; \par Stockholm (46)