\par\par \b \uc2 *S&PGR Suspends Ratings on Nigeria's \uc2 Skye Bank\b0\par\par\uc2 1,551 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Dezember 2016\par 17:46\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2016, Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2 6 Dec 2016 11:46 ET  Press Release: S&PGR Suspends Ratings on Nigeria's \uc2 Skye Bank\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par The following is a press release from \f28 \uc2 \f2 Standard & Poor's\f28 \uc2 \f2 : \par      -- We are suspending the ratings on \f28 \uc2 \f2 Skye Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2  due to a lack of sufficient, \par reliable, and timely information. \par      -- The suspension is for up to 90 days, pending the receipt of further \par information. \par  \par JOHANNESBURG (S&P Global Ratings) Dec. 6, 2016--S&P Global Ratings today \par suspended its counterparty credit ratings on \f28 \uc2 \f2 Skye Bank PLC\f28 \uc2 \f2 . \par  \par At the time of the suspension, the global and local scale ratings on \f28 \uc2 \f2 Skye Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2  \par were 'CCC-/C' and 'ngCCC-/ngC' and these ratings were on CreditWatch negative. \par  \par The suspension is based on a lack of sufficient, timely, and reliable \par information to maintain our ratings on \f28 \uc2 \f2 Skye Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2 . At mid-year 2016, the bank \par breached some regulatory ratios, including the minimum capital adequacy and \par liquidity ratios, which led the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Nigeria\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , \par suspending the bank's board of directors and changing its top management on \par July 4, 2016. Since then, the quality, quantity, and timeliness of information \par that we have received from the bank has fallen short of our requirements, \par resulting in our decision to suspend the ratings. At the time of suspension, we \par understand from our interaction with the bank's management that \f28 \uc2 \f2 Skye Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2  has \par been making timely payments on funding facilities and deposits both in U.S. \par dollars and Nigerian naira. We also understand that the bank has restructured \par some off-balance-sheet trade-related facilities under mutually agreed \par conditions with creditors. \par  \par We expect to be able to resolve the suspension within the next 90 days, subject \par to receiving the necessary information from the bank. If the information is not \par received within that timeframe, we will withdraw our ratings. \par  \par RELATED CRITERIA AND RESEARCH \par  \par Related Criteria \par      -- General Criteria: S&P Global Ratings' National And Regional Scale \par Mapping Tables - June 01, 2016 \par      -- General Criteria: National And Regional Scale Credit Ratings - \par September 22, 2014 \par      -- General Criteria: Group Rating Methodology - November 19, 2013 \par      -- Criteria - Financial Institutions - Banks: Quantitative Metrics For \par Rating Banks Globally: Methodology And Assumptions - July 17, 2013 \par      -- General Criteria: Criteria For Assigning 'CCC+', 'CCC', 'CCC-', And \par 'CC' Ratings - October 01, 2012 \par      -- Criteria - Financial Institutions - Banks: Revised Market Risk Charges \par For Banks In Our Risk-Adjusted Capital Framework - June 22, 2012 \par      -- Criteria - Financial Institutions - Banks: Banks: Rating Methodology \par And Assumptions - November 09, 2011 \par      -- Criteria - Financial Institutions - Banks: Banking Industry Country \par Risk Assessment Methodology And Assumptions - November 09, 2011 \par      -- Criteria - Financial Institutions - Banks: Bank Capital Methodology And \par Assumptions - December 06, 2010 \par      -- General Criteria: Use Of CreditWatch And Outlooks - September 14, 2009 \par      -- General Criteria: Understanding Standard & Poor's Rating Definitions - \par June 03, 2009 \par      -- Criteria - Financial Institutions - Banks: Commercial Paper I: Banks - \par March 23, 2004 \par  \par REGULATORY DISCLOSURES \par  \par      -- Primary Credit Analyst: Matthew Pirnie, Director \par      -- Rating Committee Chairperson: Mohamed Damak \par      -- Date initial rating assigned: Aug. 7, 2013 \par      -- Date of previous review: Oct. 4, 2016 \par  \par Disclaimers \par This rating has been determined by a rating committee based solely on the \par committee's independent evaluation of the credit risks and merits of the issuer \par or issue being rated in accordance with S&P Global Ratings published criteria \par and no part of this rating was influenced by any other business activities of \par S&P Global Ratings. \par  \par This credit rating is solicited. The rated entity did participate in the credit \par rating process. S&P Global Ratings did have access to the accounts, financial \par records and other relevant internal, non-public documents of the rated entity \par or a related third party. S&P Global Ratings has used information from sources \par believed to be reliable but does not guarantee the accuracy, adequacy, or \par completeness of any information used. \par  \par GLOSSARY \par  \par      -- Counterparty credit rating: A form of issuer credit rating, which is a \par forward-looking opinion about an obligor's overall creditworthiness. \par      -- Date initial rating assigned: The date S&P Global Ratings assigned the \par long-term foreign \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  issuer credit rating on the entity. \par      -- Date of previous review: The date S&P Global Ratings last reviewed the \par credit rating on the entity. \par      -- National scale rating: An opinion of an obligor's creditworthiness or \par overall capacity to meet specific financial obligations, relative to other \par issuers and issues in a given country or region. \par  \par Certain terms used in this report, particularly certain adjectives used to 