\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2-Nigeria's \uc2 Arik Air\uc2  temporarily suspends  \highlight22\uc2 operations \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 381 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 September 2016\par 23:51\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2016 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 (Adds comment from Arik on resumption of flights)\par \par \uc2 ABUJA, Sept 13 (Reuters) - \uc2 Arik Air\uc2 , Nigeria's largest airline, cancelled all flights on Tuesday in what it called a temporary disruption related to insurance renewal.\par \par \uc2 While the company initially warned the disruption was likely to continue for the next few days as it awaited approval from national insurance commission NAICOM to renew its insurance with a new company, a spokesman later told Reuters it would resume flights from 11 a.m. on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 "All issues have been resolved," spokesman Ola Adebanji said, declining to comment on how it had resolved its insurance problem or why it had changed insurance companies.\par \par \uc2 Arik, which flies to London, New York and Johannesburg, also has a maintenance contract with Germany's \uc2 Lufthansa\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "We are fully committed to returning to our normal \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  and minimize any unfortunate inconvenience to our passengers," Arik Chief Executive \uc2 Michael Arumemi-Ikhide\uc2  said in a statement on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 Nigerian airlines and international carriers operating within the country have struggled with a plunge in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the naira, that has made it difficult to get U.S. dollars to buy jet fuel and also to remain profitable as passengers pay in naira. The nation's first recession in two decades is also squeezing profits.\par \par \uc2 James Daudu, deputy director at the country's aviation ministry, said that while jet fuel prices are deregulated, and therefore outside government control, the Minister of State for Aviation was working with the \uc2 Ministry of Petroleum Resources\uc2  to see if "\b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 " in the sector were possible.\par \par \uc2 "It would be a whole sphere of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , if possible, from the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Nigeria\b0 \highlight\uc2  to the Ministry of Petroleum Resources," he said.\par \par \uc2 Two other local carriers, Aero Contractors and First Nation, recently suspended \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 , though the government said both would eventually reopen.\par \par \uc2 International carriers United and Iberia stopped their services to Nigeria earlier this year, while others have begun refuelling abroad to avoid jet fuel shortages. International airlines have complained about the difficulty of repatriating millions of dollars' worth of fares sold in local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . (Reporting by Libby George and Camillus Eboh in Abuja and Alexis Akwagyiram in Lagos; Editing by Greg Mahlich and Matthew Lewis) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2016-9-13T22:51:45.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020160913ec9d00y17\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
