\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-\uc2 Nigeria's  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight\uc2  sells dollars to lift naira off all-time low - traders\b0\par\par\uc2 328 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 August 2016\par 17:38\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2016 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 (Adds \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  sales to BDCs)\par \par \uc2 LAGOS, Aug 9 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Nigeria\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the interbank \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Tuesday to help support the naira after it hit an all-time low of 350 to the dollar in thin volume, traders said.\par \par \uc2 The naira closed at 310.50 to the dollar following the bank's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . A single trade of $100,000 was carried out at 350 to the dollar. A total of $6.86 million traded on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 The naira has been under pressure since the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  floated the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in June to allow it trade freely on the interbank market. The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been hit by a plunge in oil prices, Nigeria's economic mainstay, which caused foreign investors to flee bond and equities markets.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  last month told international money transfer operators to pay dollar proceeds from customer transfers into local commercial banks in naira, while selling the dollars themselves to bureaux de change (BDC) outlets.\par \par \uc2 On Tuesday the bank pegged the dollar transactions which banks can carry out with BDCs at $30,000 per week and set a margin for the banks to sell dollar to \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  outlets at not more than 1.5 percent over the rate at which they bought.\par \par \uc2 It hopes the move will help narrow the gulf between the official and black market rates and boost dollar liquidity, traders say.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  set a margin of two percent over the rate at which BDCs sourced dollars from banks as resale premium to customers and pegged BDC disbursement at $5,000 per transaction to cover travel allowance, medical bills and school fees.\par \par \uc2 The naira hit 400 against the dollar on the black market last week, weakened partly by dollar demand from individuals travelling abroad for their summer holidays. (Reporting by Chijioke Ohuocha; Editing by Richard Balmforth) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2016-8-9T16:38:31.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020160809ec8900tjz\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
