\par\par \b \uc2 *S&PGR Lowers \uc2 Skye Bank\uc2  To 'CCC-'; Ratings Still On Watch Neg\b0\par\par\uc2 3,137 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Juli 2016\par 18:36\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2016, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 11 Jul 2016 12:36 ET  Press Release: S&PGR Lowers \uc2 Skye Bank\uc2  To 'CCC-'; Ratings Still On Watch Neg\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par The following is a press release from \f28 \uc2 \f2 Standard & Poor's\f28 \uc2 \f2 : \par      -- We understand that Nigeria-based \f28 \uc2 \f2 Skye Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2  has breached some regulatory \par ratios, including the minimum capital adequacy and liquidity ratios. \par      -- This has lead the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Nigeria\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , suspending the \par bank's board of directors and changing its top management on July 4, 2016. \par      -- We now believe that a default of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Skye Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2  appears highly likely within \par the next six months, absent unanticipated significant favorable developments. \par      -- We are therefore are lowering our long-term global scale rating on \f28 \uc2 \f2 Skye \par Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2  to 'CCC-' from 'CCC+' and our Nigeria national scale ratings to \par 'ngCCC-/ngC' from 'ngB+/ngB'. We are placing the global scale short-term rating \par on CreditWatch negative, while maintaining the long-term ratings and national \par scale short-term rating on CreditWatch negative. \par      -- We aim to resolve the CreditWatch in the next 90 days, taking into \par account the further management or regulatory actions that may be taken with \par respect to the bank's financial sustainability. \par  \par JOHANNESBURG (S&P Global Ratings) July 11, 2016--S&P Global Ratings today \par lowered its long-term counterparty credit rating on Nigeria's \f28 \uc2 \f2 Skye Bank PLC\f28 \uc2 \f2  to \par 'CCC-' from 'CCC+' and affirmed its 'C' short-term counterparty credit rating \par on the bank. We also lowered our long- and short-term Nigeria national scale \par ratings on the bank to 'ngCCC-/ngC' from 'ngB+/ngB'. We have placed the global \par scale short-term rating on CreditWatch negative and maintained the long-term \par ratings and national scale short-term rating on CreditWatch with negative \par implications, where we placed them on June 16, 2016. \par  \par We understand that \f28 \uc2 \f2 Skye Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2  has breached regulatory ratios, including the \par minimum capital adequacy and liquidity ratios, putting marked strain on the \par bank's financial profile. In addition, the bank breached the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of \par Nigeria\f28 \uc2 \f2 's (CBN's) guideline regarding the maximum nonperforming loans ratio, \par which is also a contributing factor to the supervisory actions taken by the \par CBN. As a result, on July 4, 2016, the CBN suspended the bank's board of \par directors and senior leadership to prevent the bank's failure and the ensuing \par potential threat to the overall stability of Nigeria's financial system. We \par understand that eight board members and four executive directors, including the \par group managing director and his deputy, tendered their resignation with \par immediate effect. Furthermore, the CBN has approved the appointments of a new \par board chairman and a new managing director to oversee the management and \par potential rehabilitation of the bank. \par  \par We consider that \f28 \uc2 \f2 Skye Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2  is subject to regulatory forbearance and the breach \par of regulatory ratios will pressure its liquidity position. We now think that a \par default of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Skye Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2  within the next six months is highly likely, absent \par unanticipated significantly favorable changes in the bank's condition. At this \par stage, we understand the CBN has not yet communicated plans on how it intends \par to restore the bank's business and financial profiles. \par  \par We aim to resolve the CreditWatch in the next 90 days, depending on the further \par management or regulatory actions that may be taken with respect to \f28 \uc2 \f2 Skye Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2 's \par financial sustainability. \par  \par We could lower our ratings on the bank if we think a default is almost certain. \par This could happen if we thought that the bank was unable to make timely and \par full payment on any outstanding liabilities, due to negative regulatory \par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  or the absence of any unexpected extraordinary liquidity support. \par  \par We could affirm or raise the ratings if we were to witness an unanticipated and \par favorable transformation in \f28 \uc2 \f2 Skye Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2 's prospects, potentially through \par market-led or regulatory support, which would lead us to anticipate that a \par default is less likely within the next six months. \par  \par RELATED CRITERIA AND RESEARCH \par  \par Related Criteria \par      -- General Criteria: S&P Global Ratings' National And Regional Scale \par Mapping Tables - June 01, 2016 \par      -- General Criteria: National And Regional Scale Credit Ratings - \par September 22, 2014 \par      -- General Criteria: Group Rating Methodology - November 19, 2013 \par      -- Criteria - Financial Institutions - Banks: Quantitative Metrics For \par Rating Banks Globally: Methodology And Assumptions - July 17, 2013 \par      -- General Criteria: Criteria For Assigning 'CCC+', 'CCC', 'CCC-', And \par 'CC' Ratings - October 01, 2012 \par      -- Criteria - Financial Institutions - Banks: Revised Market Risk Charges \par For Banks In Our Risk-Adjusted Capital Framework - June 22, 2012 \par      -- Criteria - Financial Institutions - Banks: Banks: Rating Methodology \par And Assumptions - November 09, 2011 \par      -- Criteria - Financial Institutions - Banks: Banking Industry Country \par Risk Assessment Methodology And Assumptions - November 09, 2011 \par      -- Criteria - Financial Institutions - Banks: Bank Capital Methodology And \par Assumptions - December 06, 2010 \par      -- General Criteria: Use Of CreditWatch And Outlooks - September 14, 2009 \par      -- Criteria - Financial Institutions - Banks: Commercial Paper I: Banks - \par March 23, 2004 \par  \par Related Research \par      -- Banking Industry Country Risk Assessment: Nigeria - April 26, 2016 \par      -- Negative Rating Actions Taken On Six Nigerian Banks After Sovereign \par Outlook Revision - March 24, 2016 \par  \par REGULATORY DISCLOSURES \par  \par      -- Primary credit analyst: Jones Gondo, Rating Analyst \par      -- Rating committee chairperson: Mohamed Damak \par      -- Date initial rating assigned: Aug. 7, 2013 \par      -- Date of previous review: June 16, 2016 \par  \par Disclaimers \par This rating has been determined by a rating committee based solely on the \par committee's independent evaluation of the credit risks and merits of the issuer \par or issue being rated in accordance with S&P Global Ratings published criteria \par and no part of this rating was influenced by any other business activities of \par S&P Global Ratings. \par This credit rating is solicited. The rated entity did participate in the credit \par rating process. S&P Global Ratings did have access to the accounts, financial \par records and other relevant internal, non-public documents of the rated entity \par or a related third party. S&P Global Ratings has used information from sources \par believed to be reliable but does not guarantee the accuracy, adequacy, or \par completeness of any information used. \par GLOSSARY \par  \par      -- Adjusted assets: Total assets less nonservicing intangibles. \par      -- Adjusted common equity: Common shareholders' equity plus minority \par interest, minus dividends (not yet distributed), minus revaluation reserves, \par minus nonservicing intangibles, minus interest only strips, minus tax-loss \par carryforwards, minus postretirement benefit adjustments. \par      -- Anchor: The starting point for assigning a bank a long-term rating, \par based on economic and industry risk. \par      -- Asset-liability mismatch: Occurs when financial terms of an \par institution's assets and liabilities do not correspond. \par      -- Asset quality: A key measure of the quality and performance of the \par assets of a bank. \par      -- Available stable funding: Core deposits, plus deposits due to banks \par (net of those that mature within one year), plus other borrowings (net of \par maturities within one year), plus total equity, minus intangibles. \par      -- Broad liquid assets: cash (net of restricted cash) and reserves at \par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , plus other cash and money market, plus bank loans and reverse \par repos that mature in less than one year, plus total liquid assets. \par      -- Business position: A measure of the strength of a bank's business \par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . \par      -- Capital and earnings: A measure of a bank's ability to absorb losses. \par      -- Core deposits: Total deposits minus noncore deposits (such as deposits \par due to banks and certificates of deposits). \par      -- Core earnings over average managed assets: Annualized core earnings, \par over average assets of current period and last fiscal year. \par      -- Core earnings: Net income before minority interest, minus nonrecurring \par income, plus nonrecurring expenses, plus/minus tax impact on adjustments, plus \par amortization/impairment of goodwill/intangibles, minus preferred dividends. \par      -- Cost of funds: Interest expense as a percentage of average \par interest-bearing liabilities. \par      -- Counterparty credit rating: A form of issuer credit rating, which is a \par forward-looking opinion about an obligor's overall creditworthiness. \par      -- Credit losses: Losses arising from credit risk. \par      -- Credit risk: Risk that a borrower will default on its payment \par obligations. \par      -- Customer loans (gross): Total customer loans before loan loss reserves. \par      -- Customer loans (net) over customer deposits: Gross customer loans net \par of loan loss reserves, over core deposits. \par      -- Date initial rating assigned: The date S&P Global Ratings assigned the \par long-term foreign \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  issuer credit rating on the entity. \par      -- Date of previous review: The date S&P Global Ratings last reviewed the \par credit rating on the entity. \par      -- Earning capacity: The capacity of a bank to generate sufficient \par earnings against losses and the primary way that a bank builds or maintains its \par capitalization. \par      -- Earnings buffer: A measure of the capacity for earnings to absorb \par normalized losses through the credit cycle. \par      -- Fee income over operating revenues: Net income on fees and commissions \par over operating revenues. \par      -- Funding and liquidity: A combined assessment of the strength and \par stability of a bank's funding mix and its ability to manage its liquidity needs \par in adverse market and economic conditions over an extended period. \par      -- Funding base: Total deposits, plus acceptances, repurchase agreements, \par and other borrowings (including commercial papers, short- and long-term debt, \par subordinated debt, and minimal equity content hybrids). \par      -- Government-related entity (GRE) support: An assessment of the \par likelihood that the government would provide extraordinary support to a bank \par that is a government-related entity. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 11 Jul 2016 12:36 ET \par Press Release: S&PGR Lowers \f28 \uc2 \f2 Skye Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2  To 'CCC-'; -2-\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par      -- Gross nonperforming assets over customer loans plus other real estate \par owned over customer loans: Nonaccrual loans, plus restructured loans, plus \par repossessed assets plus loans 90-days past due; over gross customer loans plus \par repossessed assets. \par      -- Group support: An assessment of the likelihood that a parent or other \par group member would provide extraordinary support to a bank within that group. \par      -- Loan loss reserves over gross nonperforming assets: General plus \par specific reserves, over adjusted nonperforming assets (nonaccrual loans plus \par restructured loans plus repossessed assets plus 90-day past due loans). \par      -- Long term funding ratio: Available stable funding, over funding base \par plus total equity, minus intangibles. \par      -- National scale rating: An opinion of an obligor's creditworthiness or \par overall capacity to meet specific financial obligations, relative to other \par issuers and issues in a given country or region. \par      -- Net charge-offs over average customer loans: Gross charge-offs net of \par recoveries, over average gross customer loans of current period and last fiscal \par year. \par      -- Net interest income over operating revenues: Net interest income \par (including net interest income on loans, securities, and other assets), over \par operating revenues. \par      -- New loan loss provisions over average customer loans: Credit loss \par provisions (including specific loan provisions and general and other \par provisions) minus recoveries, over average gross customer loans of current \par period and last fiscal year. \par      -- Noninterest expenses: Salaries and general administrative expenses \par (including depreciations and amortizations). \par      -- Nonperforming loans ratio: Gross nonperforming assets over customer \par loans plus other real estate owned over customers loans: Nonaccrual loans, plus \par restructured loans, plus repossessed assets plus loans 90 days past due; over \par gross customer loans plus repossessed assets. \par      -- Normalized credit losses: An assessment of the long-term annualized \par credit-related losses expected through the credit cycle. \par      -- Operating revenues: Net interest income, plus operating non-interest \par income (that mainly includes fees and commissions and trading gains). \par      -- Preprovision operating income over average assets: Operating revenues \par minus noninterest expenses, over average assets. \par      -- Regulatory forbearance: When the regulator allows a bank to continue \par operating even though it is in breach of minimum regulatory requirements for \par its license. \par      -- Return on equity: Net income before extraordinary results minus \par preferred dividends over average common (average between current period and \par last fiscal period). \par      -- Risk position: Our view of the specific risk characteristics of a \par particular bank. \par      -- Risk-adjusted capital (RAC) ratio before diversification: This is \par calculated according to S&P Global Ratings' methodology as total adjusted \par capital over risk-adjusted assets. \par      -- Short-term wholesale funding: Debt securities that mature in less than \par one year (of commercial papers, debt and senior and subordinated bonds), plus \par bank deposits that mature in less than one year. \par      -- Sovereign support: An assessment of the likelihood that the government \par would provide extraordinary support to a bank. \par      -- Stable funding needs: Restricted cash and reserves at the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , \par plus interbank deposits, plus loans to banks (net of maturities within one \par year), plus reverse repurchase agreements, plus gross customer loans net of \par loan-loss reserves, plus securities, minus total liquid securities, plus equity \par participations in nonfinancial entities, plus fixed assets, plus other assets \par (considering foreclosed assets, tax loss carryforwards, and deferred assets). \par      -- Stable funding ratio: Available stable funding over stable funding \par needs. \par      -- Stand-alone credit profile (SACP): An interim step in assessing a \par bank's overall creditworthiness. It includes government support, but not \par extraordinary government support. \par      -- Total adjusted capital: adjusted common equity plus admissible \par preferred instruments and hybrids. \par      -- Total wholesale funding: Noncore deposits, plus acceptances, repurchase \par agreements, other borrowings (including commercial papers, debt and senior and \par subordinated bonds, minimal equity content hybrids), and total equity, minus \par minority interest and common shareholders' equity. \par  \par Certain terms used in this report, particularly certain adjectives used to \par express our view on rating relevant factors, have specific meanings ascribed to \par them in our criteria, and should therefore be read in conjunction with such \par criteria. Please see Ratings Criteria at \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.standardandpoors.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 www.standardandpoors.com}}}\uc2 \f2  for further \par information. Complete ratings information is available to subscribers of \par RatingsDirect at \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.globalcreditportal.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 www.globalcreditportal.com}}}\uc2 \f2  and at spcapitaliq.com. All ratings \par affected by this rating action can be found on S&P Global Ratings' public Web \par site at \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.standardandpoors.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 www.standardandpoors.com}}}\uc2 \f2 . Use the Ratings search box located in the \par left column. Alternatively, call one of the following S&P Global Ratings \par numbers: Client Support Europe (44) 20-