\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1- \highlight22\uc2 Nigeria central bank intervenes \highlight\uc2  with dollar sales, naira weakens\b0\par\par\uc2 379 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Juni 2016\par 16:35\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2016 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 (Adds details, naira level and traded volumes)\par \par \uc2 LAGOS, June 28 (Reuters) - \uc2 Nigeria's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has sold an undisclosed amount of hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the interbank market to ease dollar shortages and provide importers the dollars to pay for the products they bring into the country, traders said on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 The naira ended at 282.50, slightly weaker than the 281 naira to the dollar it first traded at on Tuesday, more than three hours after market opened at 0800 GMT.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been selling dollars on the interbank market since it ended its 16 month-old \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  peg last week, and it sold again on Tuesday, asking \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  traders for bid-offer quotes from them at around 1118 GMT.\par \par \uc2 A total of $51 million traded on the interbank market just before the market closed, which traders attributed to \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The old \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  peg had set a rate of 197 naira to the dollar, which over-valued the naira and led to a shortage of dollars that choked off growth in the economy. The shortage was exacerbated by plunging prices for oil, Nigeria's biggest export and its main source of hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Nigeria abandoned the peg to allow the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to trade freely on the interbank market, but lack of liquidity has curbed activity, traders say, leaving the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  as the main supplier of hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Removing the peg has narrowed the gap between naira rates available on the official and black markets. Even so, the naira was trading 20 percent lower on the unofficial market than it was on the interbank market on Tuesday, at 355 naira to the dollar.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Monday introduced an over-the-counter futures market for the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , to help manage dollar demand, quoting the naira firmer at 279 to the dollar in a month's time and at 210 naira by April next year.\par \par \uc2 In the non-deliverable forwards market, the naira rose against the dollar on Tuesday, with the one-month contract NGN1NDFOR= quoting the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  as firm as 283, after hitting 296 a week ago. (Reporting by Chijioke Ohuocha, editing by Larry King) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2016-6-28T15:35:11.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020160628ec6s00omn\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
