\par\par \b \uc2 EXCLUSIVE-Nigeria banks to set naira rate on Monday without c.bank  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  - banker\b0\par\par\uc2 324 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Juni 2016\par 20:08\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2016 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 LAGOS, June 17 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Nigeria\b0 \highlight\uc2 's commercial banks will set the first exchange rate of the naira versus the dollar when the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is allowed to float freely on Monday after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  abandoned its dollar peg, a senior banking source said on Friday.\par \par \uc2 On Wednesday, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it would float the national \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Monday, but it has given few details on how the new rules will be implemented.\par \par \uc2 In their first detailed guidance, \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  officials told bank chief executives at a meeting on Friday that lenders would set the first naira rate to the dollar based on demand without \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , one senior banking official told Reuters.\par \par \uc2 A \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  source said that Governor \uc2 Godwin Emefiele\uc2  was at the meeting and confirmed that commercial banks will determine the market rate on Monday.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  officials also told the bankers it did not commit itself to clearing up a backlog of hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  estimated at around $4 billion but will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  if needed, the banking official said.\par \par \uc2 He also said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would open up licenses for primary market dealers beyond the initial target of eight to 10 participants that it had announced on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 Bid-offer spreads for trading would be set at one naira, and banks are required to publish their buy and sell rates on a daily basis, the banking source said. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will the evaluate performance of the new regime by December, he added.\par \par \uc2 Primary dealers can handle volumes of $5 million between themselves as the standard order size and can trade up to $1 million with any other dealer, the source said.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could not be immediately reached for comment. (Reportig by Chijioke Ohuocha and Oludare Mayowa; Editing by Ulf Laessing and Hugh Lawson) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2016-6-17T19:08:18.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020160617ec6h01l3l\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
