\par\par \b \uc2 *\uc2 Nigeria's  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2  Drops  \highlight22\uc2 Foreign-Exchange \highlight\uc2  Peg\b0\par\par\uc2 211 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Juni 2016\par 16:48\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2016, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 15 Jun 2016 10:49 ET *\uc2 Nigeria's \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Pledges to Allow Naira to Trade Freely\par \par \uc2 15 Jun 2016 10:49 ET *\b \highlight22\uc2 Nigeria\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Will Still \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  Markets Periodically\par \par \uc2 15 Jun 2016 11:23 ET  Nigeria \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Drops \b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign-Exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  Peg\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par By Gbenga Akingbule and Patrick McGroarty \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ABUJA, Nigeria -- \f28 \uc2 \f2 Nigeria's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on Wednesday abandoned a \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  peg that economists and businesses long blamed for exacerbating a slide toward recession in Africa's oil-dependent top economy.\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of Nigeria Governor \f28 \uc2 \f2 Godwin Emefiele\f28 \uc2 \f2  said that beginning Monday the country's naira \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will trade at a market-determined rate rather than the 197-per-U.S. dollar level the bank has mandated for more than a year.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The black market exchange rate has shot up to around 370 naira to the dollar as the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  choked off most legal channels for procuring greenbacks. The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has been under pressure since late 2014, when oil prices began the precipitous slide that has upended Nigeria and other commodity-reliant economies across the globe.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Write to Patrick McGroarty at patrick.mcgroarty@wsj.com\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 June 15, 2016 11:23 ET (15:23 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020160615ec6f002c0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
