\par\par \b \uc2 EXCLUSIVE-\uc2 Nigerian  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight\uc2  plans sanctions against exporters -governor\b0\par\par\uc2 By Karin Strohecker   \par \uc2 507 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2015\par 18:50\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2015 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 LONDON, March 10 (Reuters) - Nigeria will enforce the repatriation of dollar-proceeds from exports and is planning sanctions against those not complying, \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor \uc2 Godwin Emefiele\uc2  told Reuters on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 Africa's largest economy has been hit hard over the past year by a steep drop in oil prices and political uncertainty over a closely fought and delayed election.\par \par \uc2 The turmoil has seen the naira lose more than 20 percent against the dollar since the middle of 2014, breaking through the important 200 per dollar level last month as it racked up the biggest monthly loss in more than five years.\par \par \uc2 In February, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  introduced trading rules under which banks will be able to purchase \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  only if they have a prior order from a corporate customer, such as a fuel importer or foreign mobile phone company looking to repatriate profits or dividends.\par \par \uc2 Now, policy makers are looking at exporters to ensure hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  liquidity within Nigeria, pondering sanctions against exporters who fail to repatriate proceeds and funnel them back into the official market within the stipulated 90-day limit, Emefiele said.\par \par \uc2 "If you refuse to sell your export proceeds that you repatriate in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market ... we will ban them from accessing \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the Nigerian \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market," Emefiele told Reuters in an interview.\par \par \uc2 Emefiele said much of the pressure on the naira over the past year was due to activity of importers and exporters, the former frontloading purchases of hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  while the latter were hoarding their overseas cash earnings.\par \par \uc2 The resulting hiatus on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets has forced the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and this has led to a steep drop in \b \highlight22\uc2 Nigeria\b0 \highlight\uc2 's foreign cash reserves to four to five months' worth of imports.\par \par \uc2 Forcing exporting and importing companies to comply with existing regulations on their use of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market was now necessary.\par \par \uc2 "Another thing we will do is that we will ask the banks not to loan money to them (exporters who don't repatriate hard cash on time)," he said, saying the measure would come into effect soon, but declining to give a date.\par \par \uc2 Emefiele estimated that some $3-4 billion of proceeds due to be repatriated were outstanding, of which 40 percent would come from oil companies.\par \par \uc2 "We are saying ... don't put your \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the hands of people who want to carry cash and take it abroad," he said. "Use it to import tangible items that are documented."\par \par \uc2 Also scrapped amid February's de facto devaluation were the bi-weekly auctions in which the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  at a predetermined rate. Emefiele said these would not be reintroduced.\par \par \uc2 "(The window) is not closed. It is crushed and destroyed for life," said Emefiele. "Nothing is going to be opened again. We are not going to go back to a subsidised regime." (Reporting by Karin Strohecker; editing by Ralph Boulton)\par \par \uc2 Released: 2015-3-13T17:50:22.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020150310eb3a00jai\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
