ght\uc2 \f2  for the third straight\par  session on Tuesday to defend the naira NGN=D1 by selling\par  dollars below its official band but the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  traded\par  weaker in the interbank market.\par                 \par  \par  NIGERIA ATTACKS\par  Explosions hit an opposition political rally in southern\par  Nigeria on Tuesday and Islamist insurgents struck in the\par  north, with unrest spreading after a presidential election\par  was postponed.\par                 \par  \par  KENYA MARKETS\par  The Kenyan shilling KES= rose against the dollar on Tuesday\par  on the back of hard \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  inflows from investors abroad\par  seeking high yields from local Treasury bonds.\par                 \par  \par  ANGOLA INFLATION\par  Angola's consumer inflation slowed slightly to 7.44 percent\par  year-on-year in January from 7.48 percent in December, data\par  from the INE statistics office showed.\par                 \par  \par      For the latest precious metals report click on        \par      For the latest base metals report click on         \par      For the latest crude oil report click on\f28 \par \par \uc2 Released: 2015-2-18T05:45:06.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020150218eb2i006my\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
