\par\par \b \uc2 WEEKAHEAD-AFRICA- \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Nigerian naira to steady on dollar sales, others seen mixed\b0\par\par\uc2 737 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 Januar 2015\par 16:55\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2015 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par LAGOS, Jan 29 (Reuters) - Nigeria's volatile naira is likely\par to steady next week on dollar sales by oil companies, while East\par African \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  are expected to be supported by \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 NIGERIA\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par     The naira is likely to trade around its present\par levels next week on the back of expected month-end dollar sales\par by some energy companies and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     The local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has remained volatile in the wake of\par falling oil price and the exit of offshore investors in local\par debt and equity last year.\par     The local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was trading around 189.90 to the dollar\par on Thursday, same level it closed a week ago. The naira was\par however weaker than its Wednesday's close of 186 after dollar\par sales from state energy company NNPC buoyed the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     NNPC sold around $350 million to some lenders on Wednesday,\par while the local unit of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Royal Dutch Shell\f28 \uc2 \f2  sold undisclosed\par dollar amounts on Thursday, keeping the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  stable.\par     Most oil companies in Africa's top crude exporter sell\par dollars to obtain local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  for their domestic obligations.\par     "We expect that the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will derive further\par support from the usual month-end oil companies' dollar sale in\par the coming days," \f28 \uc2 \f2 Citibank\f28 \uc2 \f2  said in a research note on Thursday.\par     \par     KENYA\par     Kenya's shilling is expected to trade in a tight\par range, with traders saying they were on the lookout for any\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  action that would keep it from weakening further.\par     At 0815 GMT, commercial banks quoted the shilling at\par 91.70/80 to the dollar, unchanged from last Thursday's close.\par     Last week traders said the bank sold an unspecified amount\par of dollars to keep it from going past the 91.70 level.\par     "After we saw \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  come in last week, people have\par been jittery about getting to those levels, so we are on a wait\par and see," Ian Kahangara, trader at \f28 \uc2 \f2 National Bank of Kenya\f28 \uc2 \f2 , said.\par    \par     Traders said they forecast the shilling to trade in the\par 91.70 to 92.00 range in coming days.    \par     \par     UGANDA\par     The Ugandan shilling was also seen rangebound,\par underpinned by expected \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and scarce\par local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  liquidity. \par     At 1135 GMT commercial banks quoted the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at\par 2,860/2,870, stronger than last Thursday's close of 2,880/2,890.\par     "The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has demonstrated resolve to keep the\par shilling in line... we're likely to see rangebound stability,"\par said Isaac Iga, chief dealer at Orient Bank.\par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central \f28 \b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of Uganda\f28 \uc2 \f2  (BoU) has sold dollars in the\par market five times this month to prop up the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . \par     Much of the depreciation for the shilling, which is down 3.1\par percent against the greenback this year, has been caused by\par demand from commercial banks eager to hedge against dollar.\par     Iga said the shilling would likely exchange hands in the\par 2,840-2,880 range in the coming days.\par     \par     TANZANIA\par     The shilling could weaken on dollar demand by\par importers after gaining this week from month-end hard \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par inflows.\par     Commercial banks quoted the shilling at 1,782/1,792 to the\par dollar on Thursday, stronger than 1,835/1,845 a week ago.\par     Sameer Remtulla, a dealer at Commercial Bank of Africa\par Tanzania, said the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  had "\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by selling more\par dollars to the market, but the shilling will likely be under\par pressure next week."\par     Traders expected the shilling to trade in the 1,810-1,820\par range over the coming days.\par     The \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of Tanzania\f28 \uc2 \f2  said on its website it had traded\par $52.75 million on the interbank \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market over the\par past week.\par   \par     ZAMBIA\par     The kwacha is expected to remain volatile next week\par as investors in Africa's second largest copper producer digest\par the outcome of a presidential election last week.\par     At 1115 GMT on Thursday, commercial banks quoted the kwacha\par at 6.4700 per dollar from 6.4350 a week ago.\par    "The short term outlook is for the volatility to remain quite\par substantial but to reduce as we move further from elections,"\par one commercial bank trader said.\par    Zambia's ruling party presidential candidate Edgar Lungu\par defeated his closest rival Hakainde Hichilema who said the\par election had been "stolen". \par \par  (Reporting by Oludare Mayowa, George Obulutsa, Elias\par Biryabarema, Fumbuka Ng'wanakilala and Chris Mfula; Editing by\par James Macharia)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Released: 2015-1-29T16:55:30.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020150129eb1t00huq\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
