\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2-Naira hits record lows as another  \highlight22\uc2 Nigeria \highlight\uc2  devaluation looms\b0\par\par\uc2 515 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 Januar 2015\par 14:45\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2015 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  fails to lift \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 * Oil down 38 percent since November devaluation\par \par \uc2 * Another devaluation "on the cards", analysts say (Adds analyst, closing price, background)\par \par \uc2 By Chijioke Ohuocha\par \par \uc2 LAGOS, Jan 19 (Reuters) - Nigeria's naira hit record lows against the dollar on Monday before \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  decisions that analysts say may include the second \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  devaluation in two months for Africa's top oil producer.\par \par \uc2 The naira, which has been hammered by the collapse in oil prices, fell 3.6 percent to a record low of 191.85 before recovering some ground after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , two domestic banks and an energy firm sold dollars, according to dealers.\par \par \uc2 However, it still booked its weakest close on record at 187.10 to the dollar, suggesting commercial banks in Africa's biggest economy think the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may opt for a repeat on Tuesday of its November devaluation.\par \par \uc2 Oil was at $79 a barrel on Nov. 25 when the bank lowered its target band 8 percent to 160-176 to the dollar, but since then it has dropped more than a third, exacerbating governor \uc2 Godwin Emefiele\uc2 's concerns about dwindling reserves.\par \par \uc2 Crude accounts for 95 percent of Nigeria's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 However, with national elections less than four weeks away, analysts said it was not a given that Emefiele will devalue again on Tuesday. The announcement is expected around 1330 GMT.\par \par \uc2 "Another devaluation is on the cards but the timing is still a bit unclear," said Ridle Markus, a sub-Saharan Africa \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Barclays Africa in Johannesburg.\par \par \uc2 According to its website, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  spent $28 million a day last year trying and failing to defend the naira, which dropped 13.2 percent during 2014, including the one-off official devaluation.\par \par \uc2 Foreign reserves stood at $34.5 billion last week, a drop of 20 percent over the year.\par \par \uc2 Compounding Abuja's problems, \uc2 JP Morgan\uc2  said last week it was re-assessing Nigeria's inclusion in its key emerging market bond index, putting a question mark over one of the government's few non-oil sources of funding.\par \par \uc2 "The reversal of inflows, coupled with a falling oil price in a low \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves environment, implies a sizeable naira depreciation is coming," said Yvonne Mhango, an economist at Renaissance Capital in Johannesburg.\par \par \uc2 "This may be in the form of a second devaluation... or through the loosening of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's hold on the naira," she added.\par \par \uc2 Further unsettling the outlook, a deepening insurgency in the northeast by Islamist group \uc2 Boko Haram\uc2  is adding to the tensions that have preceded every election since the end of military rule 15 years ago.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is expected to keep its main interest rate on hold at 13 percent, having raised it a hefty 100 basis points in November in an attempt to draw a line under the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's weakness. (Reporting by Chijioke Ohuocha, Oludare Mayowa and Ed Cropley; Writing by Ed Cropley; Editing by Dominic Evans/Ruth Pitchford) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2015-1-19T14:45:52.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020150119eb1j009tw\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
