\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Nigeria naira down 1.2 pct despite cenbank dollar sale\b0\par\par\uc2 321 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Januar 2015\par 15:28\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2015 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 (Adds naira close, comment from dealer, cbank \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 )\par \par \uc2 LAGOS, Jan 15 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Nigeria\b0 \highlight\uc2 's naira fell 1.2 percent to close at 185.60 to the greenback on Thursday, despite the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  with dollar sales to try to prop up the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said.\par \par \uc2 The unit opened at 183.40 naira to the greenback, the same level it closed at the previous day. But quickly weakened to an intraday low of 186.30 naira in thin trade, prompting the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said.\par \par \uc2 The bank on Thursday asked 21 commercial lenders to bid for $500,000 each, in an \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  move aimed at providing liquidity to the interbank market and supporting the naira, which has been hard hit by falling global oil prices.\par \par \uc2 "I think \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will try to control any uptrend in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , to provide liquidity to the market. But for how long is the question," one dealer said.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was forced to devalued the naira two months ago to halt the slides in its foreign reserves, after the country's main export commodity, oil plunged. The bank devalued the naira by 8 percent and tightened trading rules to try to curb speculation against the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 But the naira has traded well outside its devalued band of 160-176 - and reserves are still falling.\par \par \uc2 Nigeria's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves on Jan. 13 were down 3.2 percent month-on-month from December to $34.51 billion by Jan. 13 because of drawdowns to defend the naira, \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  data showed.\par \par \uc2 At a separate dollar sale, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold $249 million to lenders at 168 naira at its twice-weekly \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  auction on Wednesday to help meet demand for the greenback, higher than the $200 million it earlier offered. (Reporting by Chijioke Ohuocha) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2015-1-15T15:28:53.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020150115eb1f00foo\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
